  "result": "All 1419 tests pass. The fix resolves the issue.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe problem: `CliRunner`'s `isolation()` context manager backs `sys.stdout`/`sys.stderr` with `io.BytesIO`-based buffers (`BytesIOCopy`), which don't support `fileno()`. Code under test that passes these streams to `subprocess.run(..., stdout=sys.stderr)` fails with `io.UnsupportedOperation: fileno`.\n\nFix in `src/click/testing.py`: `BytesIOCopy` now lazily backs itself with a real `tempfile.TemporaryFile()` the first time `fileno()` is called, moving previously-captured bytes into it and keeping subsequent reads/writes/`getvalue()` in sync with whichever backing store is active. This keeps the common case (`io.BytesIO`, no real file descriptor, no leak risk) unchanged while making `fileno()` \u2014 and thus APIs like `subprocess.run` \u2014 work when actually needed. `close()` was overridden to also close the real file when present, so garbage collection doesn't leak file descriptors.\n\nVerified with the issue's reproduction case plus the full test suite (1419 passed, 24 skipped, 1 xfailed, no regressions, no resource warnings).",
